[[12028,4648,"When Mr Gonzalez Barrén lost consciousness, there was a delay before it was recognised that this was not part of the performance","delayed recognition of unconsciousness",""],[12029,4648,"She did not appreciate that there would be non native English (mostly Spanish) speakers working the event, which might raise language barriers in an emergency","lack of language barrier awareness",""],[12030,4648,"She did not know the protocol for ringing an ambulance","unknown ambulance protocol",""],[12031,4648,"The first aider did not take the defibrillator with her when she first went to the ring","defibrillator not retrieved promptly",""],[12032,4648,"When Mr Gonzalez Barron collapsed, the scene was chaotic. No person took charge","lack of leadership during emergency",""],[12033,4648,"Chest compressions were started two minutes after that, at 10.22pm. CPR should have been started as soon as Mr Gonzalez Barrén arrested","delayed CPR initiation",""]]